course: dictionary
lesson: 11813
title: Bidding: offers and orders
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Mum raised her hand at the auction and joined the bidding for the old clock.» Bidding here means offering money to buy something. An auction is a sale where things go to the person who offers the most. Each new offer is a bid.
explain: «The little robot did its master's bidding without a single word.» Here bidding is an old word for orders. The robot did what its master told it to do. Ask yourself: is someone giving commands? If yes, bidding means orders or requests.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. «She went to bed at her mother's bidding» means she went because her mother told her to. Bidding is also a verb, as in «I am bidding you goodnight», an old-fashioned way of saying goodbye.
fact: Bidding can be a noun or a verb. The verb forms are bid, bids, bid and bidding.
fact: At an auction, the highest bid wins the item.
fact: «Do someone's bidding» means to do what they tell you to do.
fact: A bidding war happens when two buyers keep offering more and more money for the same thing.
fact: In card games, bidding means saying how many tricks you think you can win.
exercise: «Everyone raised their paddles during the bidding for the painting.» What is the bidding? | *Offering money at an auction | Hiding something under a table | Singing a loud song | Running a race
exercise: «The little robot did its master's bidding without a word.» What does do its master's bidding mean? | Ate its dinner early | *Did what its master told it to do | Ran away from home | Built a new master
exercise: In a card game, Sam says he is bidding four. What does this mean? | He has four cards in his hand | *He thinks he can win four tricks | He is four years old | He wants four cookies
test: «The bids rose quickly until one buyer won the vase.» What does bids mean here? | Shouts of joy | *Offers of money | Dirty marks | Dances
test: Which phrase means to do what someone tells you? | *Do someone's bidding | Bidding war | Bidding goodnight | Open the bidding
exam: «The bidding war made the price of the old bike double.» Why did the price go up? | Sellers kept asking for less | *Buyers kept offering more money | Nobody wanted it | The bike was stolen
